From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abhay-byte <abhay02delhi@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 22:30:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] panvk: emulate BC unless every BC format is native

panvk_bc_emul_enabled() turned BC emulation off as soon as kbase
TEXTURE_FEATURES reported BC1. Mali-G57 (v9) and Mali-G610 (v10) report
BC1 without the other BC formats, so emulation went off while
has_texture_compression_bc() still wanted all of them natively:
textureCompressionBC stayed false, every BC format had no features, and
DXVK skipped the adapter ("Device does not support required feature
'textureCompressionBC'").

Keep emulation on unless all ten BC formats (mask 0x1ff80) are native.
When emulation is off, BC formats now take the native per-format path in
get_image_plane_format_features() instead of returning 0. Image creation
(panvk_image_init), image views, meta copies and the feature bit all use
panvk_bc_emul_enabled(), so they stay consistent. GPUs without native BC1
(G615, G720, G925) are unchanged.

Purpose: expose textureCompressionBC on v9 G57 and v10 G610 (DXVK adapter selection)

Tested GPU: Mali-G57 MC2 (Lenovo TB336FU, 0x90930010, PAN_ARCH 9 JM)
Tested Kbase UAPI: JM 11.0
Mesa base range: 5a07217f034b (26.3.0-devel)
Validation test: deqp-vk via shim on G57: info.device_features textureCompressionBC 0 -> 1; api.info.format_properties.bc* 16/16 pass; texture.compressed BC fails match native ETC2-RGBA/ASTC fails on v9 (pre-existing v9 sampling issue)

Generated-by: LLM

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_physical_device.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_physical_device.c
index 7aa9d6abea21198cfe9557895e52fc2bcb36356a..a56fe757f247cdda93223102e77f54c4be92f5d0 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_physical_device.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_physical_device.c
@@ -1817,12 +1817,26 @@ panvk_bc_emul_enabled(const struct panvk_physical_device *physical_device)
    if (PANVK_DEBUG(NO_BC_EMUL))
       return false;

-   const struct pan_format fmt =
-      physical_device->formats.all[PIPE_FORMAT_DXT1_RGBA];
+   /* Emulate unless every BC format is native. Some v9/v10 kbase GPUs
+    * (G57, G610) report BC1 alone; keying off BC1 disabled emulation there
+    * and left textureCompressionBC false with no usable BC format. */
+   static const enum pipe_format bc_fmts[] = {
+      PIPE_FORMAT_DXT1_RGBA,       PIPE_FORMAT_DXT3_RGBA,
+      PIPE_FORMAT_DXT5_RGBA,       PIPE_FORMAT_RGTC1_UNORM,
+      PIPE_FORMAT_RGTC1_SNORM,     PIPE_FORMAT_RGTC2_UNORM,
+      PIPE_FORMAT_RGTC2_SNORM,     PIPE_FORMAT_BPTC_RGB_FLOAT,
+      PIPE_FORMAT_BPTC_RGB_UFLOAT, PIPE_FORMAT_BPTC_RGBA_UNORM,
+   };
    uint32_t supported_compr_fmts =
       pan_query_compressed_formats(&physical_device->kmod.dev->props);

-   return !(BITFIELD_BIT(fmt.texfeat_bit) & supported_compr_fmts);
+   for (unsigned i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(bc_fmts); i++) {
+      const struct pan_format fmt = physical_device->formats.all[bc_fmts[i]];
+      if (!fmt.hw || !(BITFIELD_BIT(fmt.texfeat_bit) & supported_compr_fmts))
+         return true;
+   }
+
+   return false;
 }

 static VkFormatFeatureFlags2
@@ -1834,10 +1848,8 @@ get_image_plane_format_features(struct panvk_physical_device *physical_device,
    const struct pan_format fmt = physical_device->formats.all[pfmt];
    unsigned arch = pan_arch(physical_device->kmod.dev->props.gpu_id);

-   if (panvk_format_is_bc(format)) {
-      if (!panvk_bc_emul_enabled(physical_device))
-         return 0;
-
+   /* Without emulation, BC formats take the native per-format path below. */
+   if (panvk_format_is_bc(format) && panvk_bc_emul_enabled(physical_device)) {
       features = VK_FORMAT_FEATURE_2_TRANSFER_SRC_BIT |
                  VK_FORMAT_FEATURE_2_TRANSFER_DST_BIT |
                  VK_FORMAT_FEATURE_2_SAMPLED_IMAGE_BIT |
